{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_10","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Closed a visible asymmetry in the read path. The leader's ReadIndex handler treats two rejections differently: the branch for a leader with no committed entry in its term reports the context as dropped, while the branch for a requester recorded as a witness only logs and returns. That would matter if a witness could get a read registered, because the caller would be left to its deadline instead of learning the operation is invalid. Tracing admission shows it cannot: the node's read entry point checks initialization and then rejects a witness with an invalid-operation error before any request state is created, and the host's linearizable-read path goes through that entry point. A witness therefore sees an immediate error, and the raft-layer branch stays a defence-in-depth path with no in-tree producer behind it. Recorded as one Behavior and one source-only, defect-refuting account, with the remaining asymmetry, the configuration-versus-membership role disagreement and the direct-peer-call caveat kept as counterevidence and limits.\"}"}}
